<!--
  The source of Kalyta/Resources/Autopay.shortcut: one "Add Expense" action whose Amount is the
  Shortcut Input's Amount and whose Note is its Merchant, for a Wallet Transaction automation.

  The action dictionary is copied from a shortcut built in the Shortcuts app on the simulator
  (the AppIntentDescriptor, the action identifier <bundle id>.<intent type>, the parameter
  keys = the intent's property names). "Amount" and "Merchant" are the transaction's content
  property names from ContentKit. The bundle identifier must match the installed app.

  After editing, sign it again (macOS signs through iCloud, see `man shortcuts`):
      shortcuts sign mode anyone input scripts/autopay-shortcut.plist output Kalyta/Resources/Autopay.shortcut
  (each option with its two leading dashes; XML comments cannot contain them).
-->
